  "notes": "S1 slow button press diagnostics, thresholds copied from s0_acceptance.json where analogous. The press is 200 constant-force phases of 10 ms ramping the button actuator 0 to -25 N (negative presses, -X), then 1.0 s at -25 N, a 0.5 s zero-input release and a 1.5 s final hold. rod_full_stroke passes when the rod displacement is within [-24.5, -21.939] mm, i.e. at least 95% of the 23.094 mm stroke (the stop is at -23.194 mm). body_drop_total_* are signed world-z changes since the initial pose (S0 bound +/-0.1 mm); body_drop_extra_* are since the end of settle. window=max_over_phase covers only the named to_phase, so the press is sampled at its last ramp phase press_199 and the pressed hold. contact_duration is whole-run (it includes settle), so it is not a press-only metric. 0.2 mm peak penetration is the numerical validity bound, never a physical FAIL. Packet diagnostics (packet_*): one free 165 x 55 x 5.2 mm packet sits in the magazine. packet_pushed_x_* is the packet's X displacement in the body frame since the end of settle (how far the press pushes it, signed +X), bounded only by +/-0.2 m so it reports min/max evidence rather than gating. packet_pose_* is its full relative pose to body (diagnostic bound 0.5 m / pi rad). packet_world_z_* is the signed world-z change of the packet relative to the housing (a large negative value means it fell out). packet_settled is body_speed at the final hold.",
